\ **************************************************************************
\ *
\ *     spare.6502 - six of the pool's pages, in the spare (D13)
\ *
\ **************************************************************************
\
\ Zeroed by start. The pool is a page a field, indexed by piece (1..255; 0
\ is the C's null piece), each page standing alone: six live here, where
\ nothing else ever writes, p_co and p_yf in BSS, and p_next, which only
\ the capture reads, in the junk row above B (scratch.6502).

.p_x0   SKIP 256                ; first column
.p_x1   SKIP 256                ; one past the last
.p_y0   SKIP 256                ; the row at x0
.p_glo  SKIP 256                ; the gradient: its fraction...
.p_ghi  SKIP 256                ; ...and its sign (bit 7) and whole rows
.p_ce   SKIP 256                ; the colour's even pattern (odd: p_co, in BSS)
